cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Quoridor frontier research"
message: "Please cite this repository if you use the solver or the 3x9 frontier results."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Napoly
    given-names: Ulysse
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible computational proof searches reporting first-player wins for
  3x9 Quoridor with 9 and 10 walls per player. Matching conservative upper-
  and lower-bound audits establish an exact 35-ply minimax forcing horizon
  for the 10-wall case, with reference move-generation and bounded-search
  differential tests and archived raw logs.
